# Context7 for External Dependencies

RULE: Append "use context7" to prompts involving external libraries, APIs, or frameworks to get up-to-date docs.
WHY: External library APIs change; context7 provides current documentation and examples, preventing use of deprecated patterns.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/dependency-management.md

DO:
  "Optimize pandas aggregation for tick data use context7"
  "How to use aiohttp session pooling use context7"
  "NautilusTrader order submission pattern use context7"

USE FOR:
  Market data APIs (Tardis, Databento, The Graph, Alchemy)
  Cloud providers (GCP, AWS — storage, pubsub, secret manager)
  ML frameworks (LightGBM, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn)
  Trading engines (NautilusTrader)
  Any external package where version-specific behavior matters
